      {
        "id": 128078,
        "name": "arenson9",
        "username": "arenson9",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/arenson9/{size}/1900_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-20T17:36:12.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Rabit\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/rabit/48/5774_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Rabit:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Powerhound_2000 wrote:</b><br><blockquote>My speculation is that the next expansion may be the last and so it gets an oversized card for being special.&nbsp;\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nOr a completely different play style that doesn't require villain character cards like we've seen before...\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I think this is probably the right track.</p>\n<p>I don't have a reference, but I think GtG have announced that the last expansion will, like Vengeance, add a new playstyle.</p>\n<p>We're being told that the next Oversized Villains pack will have a card for all villains, which means we might not get any new villain decks.</p>\n<p>I believe that as of the WCos release, every hero has a nemesis in the Vengeance decks, so I think it's possible we simply won't get any more heroes.</p>\n<p>If no new hero decks are coming, no new villain decks are coming, and the last expansion provides a new play style, it could be something very different from what we've seen before.&nbsp;</p>\n<p>In case anyone's wondering, I have no insider knowledge on this. I could be way off base.</p>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>",
