      {
        "id": 128084,
        "name": "MrLeRobot",
        "username": "MrLeRobot",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/mrlerobot/{size}/1932_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-21T02:53:42.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>If I may allow myself to take a huge wild guess on what could make the final expansion, I'd say this:</p><p>Campaign Mode</p><p>I saw a lot of fan made campaign for SotM. I even started creating my own sorta storyline to go through all of the villain, but with an added flavor, just for fun. I had a lot of fun just imagining how villains show up and why they're there and how the heroes would respond... I can't imagine Christopher NOT doing this kind of exercise. Thinking about it, I know he did. Heck, he's got like 30 years worth of storyline written down in his head (and also inside a notebook if I'm not mistaken?)... I know I'd personnally be all the way into a big multi-session campaign of SotM, with each match influencing the outcome of the rest of the whole story. Perhaps, there could even be some special cards, not included in a particular deck, with a special power a hero would start every game with, ala \"Pathfinder Adventure Card Game\"? You've beaten Ambuscade? \"Hey, look how sweet those custom handguns look like...\" Expatriette tells herself. \"Maybe I should bring those to my next fight, 'cause you know, you never have too much guns...\". Even the Big Bad could be a multi-match battle. Kind of like \"You think you've beat me... Now, witness my true form and despair!\"</p><p>Anyone?</p>",
