        "avatar_template": "/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/t/da6949/{size}.png",
        "created_at": "2015-01-21T03:40:46.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>One year ago, I began taking note on how a \"campaign game\" using cards could work. Heroes had varying skills (recruit, patrol, investigate, science, etc), and you used your recruited heroes to solve \"problem\" cards (Crime wave ! 3 patrol point to solve. Framed Hero ! Ned investigate and charisma, etc) or gain ressources for upgrading your HQ / weakening villains. Some of the \"problems\" (and \"tracks\" reaching a given point) did activate a Villain Fight using SotM. But I never thought before to give this a \"goal\" like defeating a greater menace (maybe by building a big Doctor McGuffin's Neutralizer ?) or preventing FILTER or other organizations from doing something bad - a \"scenario\".</p><p>I certainly would like to see something like that published by &gt;G someday :)</p>",
